#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Debugging/Testing/CLI.rst:15
msgid "Running Tests in ROS 2 from the Command Line - how-to"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Debugging/Testing/CLI.rst:18
msgid ""
"Running tests from the command line helps verify that ROS packages build "
"correctly and behave as expected. This article explains how to run package "
"tests with ``colcon``, examine test results, and find guidance for debugging "
"failing tests. After following these steps, you will be able to run tests, "
"filter packages, view failures, and find debugging guidance."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Debugging/Testing/CLI.rst:28
msgid "Contents"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Debugging/Testing/CLI.rst:31
msgid "Prerequisites"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Debugging/Testing/CLI.rst:33
msgid "You will need a workspace setup with packages that have tests in them."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Debugging/Testing/CLI.rst:36
msgid "Build and run your tests"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Debugging/Testing/CLI.rst:38
msgid ""
"To compile and run the tests, simply run the `test <https://colcon."
"readthedocs.io/en/released/reference/verb/test.html>`__ verb from ``colcon`` "
"at the root of your workspace."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Debugging/Testing/CLI.rst:40
msgid "$ colcon test --ctest-args tests [package_selection_args]"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Debugging/Testing/CLI.rst:44
msgid ""
"Where ``package_selection_args`` are optional package selection arguments "
"for ``colcon`` to limit which packages are built and run. Find more info in "
"the `colcon documentation on Package selection arguments <https://colcon."
"readthedocs.io/en/released/reference/package-selection-arguments.html>`__"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Debugging/Testing/CLI.rst:47
msgid ""
":ref:`Sourcing the workspace <colcon-tutorial-source-the-environment>` "
"before testing should not be necessary. ``colcon test`` makes sure that the "
"tests run with the right environment, have access to their dependencies, etc."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Debugging/Testing/CLI.rst:51
msgid "Examine Test Results"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Debugging/Testing/CLI.rst:53
msgid ""
"To see the results, simply run the `test-result <https://colcon.readthedocs."
"io/en/released/reference/verb/test-result.html>`__ verb from ``colcon``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Debugging/Testing/CLI.rst:55
msgid "$ colcon test-result --all"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Debugging/Testing/CLI.rst:59
msgid "To see the exact test cases which fail, use the ``--verbose`` flag:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Debugging/Testing/CLI.rst:61
msgid "$ colcon test-result --all --verbose"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Debugging/Testing/CLI.rst:66
msgid "Debugging tests with GDB"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Debugging/Testing/CLI.rst:68
msgid ""
"For detailed guidance on debugging tests using GDB, refer to the :doc:`GDB "
"Tutorial <../Getting-Backtraces-in-ROS-2>`."
msgstr ""
